  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "arXiv:math/0501112v3 [math.CO] 31 May 2005 — We study asymptotics of reducible representations of the symmetric groups Sq for large q.\n\n**arXiv:math/0501112v3 [math.CO] 31 May 2005**\n\n*PIOTR ŚNIADY*\n\n37 pp, 39 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We study asymptotics of reducible representations of the symmetric groups Sq for large q. We decompose such a representation as a sum of irreducible components (or, alternatively, Young diagrams) and we ask what is the character of a randomly chosen component (or, what is the shape of a randomly chosen Young diagram). Our main result is that for a large class of representations the ﬂuctuations of characters (and ﬂuctuations of the shape of the Young diagrams) are asymptoti- cally Gaussian; in this way we generalize Kerov’s central limit theorem. The considered class consists of representations for which the characters almost factorize and this class includes, for example, left-regular repre- sentation (Plancherel measure), tensor representations. This class is also closed under induction, restriction, outer product and tensor product of representations.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Representations of large symmetric groups; 1.2 Genus expansion, random matrices and free ; 1.3 Higher-order free probability; 1.4 Factorization of characters; 1.5 Fluctuations of Young diagrams; 1.6 Overview of this article; 2 Preliminaries; 2.2 Disjoint product; 2.3 Classical cumulants; 2.4 Elements of the group algebra as random va; 2.5 Canonical probability measure on Young dia; 2.6 Generalized Young diagrams; 2.7 Functionals of the shape of Young diagrams; 2.8 Transition measure of a Young diagram; 2.9 Free cumulants of the transition measure; 3 Representations with character factorization",
